:"What is Djerba known for?","a":"A Mediterranean island of beaches and thalassotherapy spas, the UNESCO island landscape of whitewashed villages, and El Ghriba - one of the oldest synagogues on Earth. A soft-adventure counterpoint to the medina and the Sahara.","source":"carthagemagazine.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Djerba?","a":"April-June and September-October - warm sea and fewer crowds. July-August is peak European beach season; December-February is mild, quiet and cheapest.","source":"lonelyplanet.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Can I combine Djerba with the rest of Tunisia?","a":"Yes - it''s the beach-and-wellness leg. Pair it with Tunis and Carthage (culture) and the Sahara oases (Tozeur/Douz) for the whole country in one loop.","source":"carthagemagazine.com","si_tag":"wellness"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Djerba Guide: Beaches, Thalassotherapy & El Ghriba - Best Time & Safety","meta_description":"Plan Djerba - Mediterranean beaches, thalassotherapy spas, the UNESCO island landscape and the El Ghriba synagogue, best season Apr-Jun & Sep-Oct, with real safety and timing intel.","slug":"djerba-tunisia","primary_keyword":"Djerba Tunisia","long_tail":["Djerba beaches","Djerba thalassotherapy","El Ghriba synagogue","Djerba UNESCO","is Djerba safe","best time to visit Djerba"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Djerba","El Ghriba","thalasso","Houmt Souk","Guellala"],"hreflang":["en","fr","ar"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-03","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-03","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Develo